agent_0.revised_operationalization:
After the bag is sealed, the fisher places any excess fish in the shared bucket. At the end of the trip, a council‑appointed observer or designated volunteer will:
1) Verify the bucket’s contents;
2) Release each fish back into the lake gently, ensuring they remain alive;
3) Record the release action, the number of fish returned, and note whether the release is part of an approved exemption with its expiry date, in the ledger;
4) Return to the shore within 30 minutes of the fisher’s arrival to minimize stress on the fish. This process is repeated daily for all trips and ensures the community’s shared resource is respected.

